From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 20:35:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 137/342] meson_vdec: HEVC, a feasibility test (experimental)

The S905's HEVC block, with linux-firmware's gxl_hevc.bin
(MESON_VDEC_HEVC) or the vendor kernel's microcode
(MESON_VDEC_HEVC_VENDOR): power, clock, firmware, the stream parser
feeding the block's stream buffer, the codec start; the firmware parses
each slice header and the host programs an intra slice's decoding to NV12
(64 KB aligned planes: the GXBB's reference table keeps address bits 31:16
only). Intra pictures of 8-bit streams only; the others are skipped. The
mailbox interrupt stays masked, the waits poll. On the ODROID-C2, 320x240
and 1920x1080 intra streams match FFmpeg bit for bit, with either
firmware. Facts: the port's docs/m26-vdec-hevc-facts.md and
docs/m26-vdec-hevc-vendor-facts.md.

The class, its registers and constants move to meson_vdec_private.h for
the second source file. The parser submit's trace reads the level of the
block in use: reading VDEC_1's registers while it is powered down (an HEVC
session) hangs the bus.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
